    "https://www.cofo.edu/Academics/Career-Services": {
      "title": "Career Services",
      "description": "Career Services | Academics | Hard Work U. Skip Navigation to Content Campusweb Keeter Center Ralph Foster Museum Lab School K-12 Campus Store Athletics Search Apply About Accolades & Accreditation Meet President Johnson and First Lady Laura Johnson Consumer Information Events & Community Programs Human Resources Hard Work U. News FAQs Admissions Virtual Tour Apply Request Information Admission Criteria Graduate Debt-Free Timeline & Interview Campus Life Cost & Financial Aid Counselor Tool Box Academics Majors & Minors Pre-Professional Resources Library College Catalog Student Handbook Registrar's Office Career Services Faithful Lives Pillars Academic Christian Cultural Patriotic Vocational Visit Welcome Video Sights to See Famous Visitors Campus Store The Keeter Center S of O Lab School Alumni Alumni Giving Join or Update Alumni News Alumni Chapters Meritorious Awards Request Transcript Lake Honor Restoration Project Give Give Online Associates Planned Giving Request Info PhilanthroCorp Estate Services Apply Search Academics - Career Services About Accolades & Accreditation Meet President Johnson and First Lady Laura Johnson Consumer Information Events & Community Programs Human Resources Hard Work U. News FAQs Admissions Virtual Tour Apply Request Information Admission Criteria Graduate Debt-Free Timeline & Interview Campus Life Cost & Financial Aid Counselor Tool Box Academics Majors & Minors Pre-Professional Resources Library College Catalog Student Handbook Registrar's Office Career Services Faithful Lives Pillars Academic Christian Cultural Patriotic Vocational Visit Welcome Video Sights to See Famous Visitors Campus Store The Keeter Center S of O Lab School Alumni Alumni Giving Join or Update Alumni News Alumni Chapters Meritorious Awards Request Transcript Lake Honor Restoration Project Give Give Online Associates Planned Giving Request Info PhilanthroCorp Estate Services Apply Campusweb Keeter Center Ralph Foster Museum Lab School K-12 Campus Store Athletics The Vocation Center is committed to student success, and assists students with academic major/minor selection and the development of professional pathways. Additionally, we offer assistance with career assessments, résumés, cover letters, LinkedIn, and developing interview skills. The Vocation Center also helps students find part-time jobs and internships that will help them gain the necessary experience for future employment. Coaching with the director is available by appointment. Vocation Center hours are Monday-Friday, 8:00 AM- 5:00 PM. Contact us at career@cofo.edu or 417-690-3248 Visit the FAQ s for more information. Want to hire our students? Send job descriptions directly to our office email: career@cofo.edu Temporary Jobs (i.e., babysitting, moving assistance, yard work) Please call or email us at 417-690-3248, career@cofo.edu Fall 2026 CAREER EXPO - September 23, 2026 (10:00 a.m. to 2:00 p.m.) Our Purpose We help students to understand the deep and rich biblical expression of \"Vocation\" and how to utilize this understanding through their \"Callings,” thus transitioning into the marketplace with a healthy, mission-minded approach. We love to hear our Alumni's success stories. Contact us and let us know about any major promotions and accomplishments so we can highlight you to our students! Summer & Seasonal job fair\r\n(Dates dropping soon) The annual Vocation Trip is an experience designed to help students explore their vocation and prepare for life after graduation. During the trip, students travel to a major city where they connect with alumni, business leaders, nonprofits, and organizations to gain career insight and professional experience. Students participate in networking opportunities, career development workshops, TED-style talks, and visits to businesses and community organizations while refining skills such as interviewing, résumé building, LinkedIn, and networking. The trip encourages students to discover their strengths, grow in confidence, and reflect on how their personal calling and career path align with their values and purpose. Vocation Center Director Candace Stark is the Director of the Vanek Center for Vocation and Callings at College of the Ozarks. She is deeply committed to serving students and dedicated to supporting their success in their academic, professional, and personal journeys.  Her professional mission is to equip the next generation with the knowledge, confidence, and tools needed to pursue their vocations and make meaningful contributions to their communities. She thrives on leading initiatives that prepare students for lives of impact, purpose, and service. Administrative Assistant Sarah Williams is the Administrative Assistant of the Vanek Center for Vocation and Callings. An alumna of College of the Ozarks, she is happy to build relationships and provide guidance to students who come looking for it as well as the ones she supervises at the Vanek Center. Student Associates Caleb Martin is a junior double-majoring in Marketing and Business Management and Savannah Mosher is a sophomore majoring in Psychology. Skip to Top of Page © 2026 College of the Ozarks Mailing Address: P.O. Box 17, Point Lookout, MO 65726 Physical Address: 1 Opportunity Ave., Point Lookout, MO 65726 Main Number: 1.800.222.0525 Contact Student Achievement Accessibility Terms Of Use Login"
    },
    "https://www.cofo.edu/Portals/0/Accolades/7def0b94-1f28-4661-bf1e-1145b0065de9.pdf?ver=M7JGMf8SRzCk437-oRlGMA%3d%3d": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Computer Science",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Computer Science  \nCollege of the Ozarks invites applications for a full-time faculty position in Computer Science \nbeginning in the Fall 2027 semester, though starting Spring 2027 may be possible.  We seek a \nstudent-centered, self-motivated, and versatile faculty member with strong teaching skills and a \ndemonstrated ability to collaborate and communicate effectively with colleagues. This position \nwill focus primarily on the continued development and stewardship of our new Data Science \nand Artificial Intelligence program.  \nThe Computer Science Department offers majors and minors in Computer Information Science, \nComputer Science, and Data Science and Artificial Intelligence, as well as a minor in \nCybersecurity and a range of general education courses.  \nTeaching responsibilities will include both lower- and upper-division courses in Computer \nScience, Data Science, and Artificial Intelligence. The successful candidate will also be expected \nto maintain and develop course content and curriculum to ensure high-quality instruction and \nongoing alignment with academic standards and industry needs. The standard teaching load is \n24 credit hours over a nine-month academic year .  \nCollege of the Ozarks is a distinctive liberal arts, work-study college of approximately 1,450 \nstudents, located in southwest Missouri near Branson. Deeply rooted in Christian faith and \nservice, the College is known for its close-knit community, strong mentoring culture, and \ncommitment to developing students academically, professionally, and spiritually. Class sizes are \nintentionally small, typically 10 to 25 students in STEM courses, allowing faculty to build \nmeaningful relationships with students.  \nCollege of the Ozarks seeks faculty members who embrace the institution’s Christian mission, \ndemonstrate excellence in undergraduate teaching, serve as mentors and positive role models \nfor students, and contribute collaboratively to the life of the College. Applicants should hold an \nM.S., D.Sc., or Ph.D. in Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related computing field. \nCandidates with degrees in a related discipline should also demonstrate substantial, well-\ndocumented experience in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence.  \nTo apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, transcripts, and three letters of \nrecommendation, including one from your pastor, to Dr. Susan DeWoody, Provost, PO Box 17, \nPoint Lookout, MO 65726, or by email to provostoffice@cofo.edu. Review of applications will \nbegin immediately and continue until the position is filled. "
    },
    "https://www.cofo.edu/Portals/0/Accolades/e3a52c4c-2c93-4875-9cdf-a2388762b6fe.pdf?ver=8zY66Qqmv3JYCMNuTMPHWw%3d%3d": {
      "title": "College of the Ozarks invites applicants for a part-time, adjunct faculty position in",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Applied Music \n College of the Ozarks invites applicants for a part-time, adjunct faculty position in \ninstrumental private lesson instruction.  \nCollege of the Ozarks is committed to hiring faculty members who embrace the \ninstitution’s Christian mission, pursue excellence in teaching undergraduate students, and \nserve as mentors and positive role models. Faculty are expected to be self-motivated and \nversatile, with strong communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively with other \nfaculty and staff. Primary responsibilities for this position include teaching private lessons \nin woodwinds, brass, guitar, or percussion, as well as instructing a methods class suited to \nthe instructor’s particular area of expertise. \nCandidates should hold a master’s degree in music and/or possess considerable \nperformance experience. Undergraduate teaching experience is a plus. College of the \nOzarks is a Christian liberal arts college with a commitment to faith-based education. The \ncampus is in Point Lookout, MO, near Branson.  \nTo apply, please address a letter of application to Dr. Susan DeWoody and send the letter \nand CV to Andrea Oliver at provostoffice@cofo.edu. Review of applications begins \nimmediately, with placement dependent upon credentials and current course needs. "
    },
